turnkey-nodebb-19.0 (2) turnkey; urgency=low

  * The build proves that the project archive it installs from is the live
    one. bin/keel-archive-check compares the package index copied into the
    build tree with the index of the archive on the build host and stops the
    build when they differ: in bootstrap/post, where the copy is made, and
    again on the tree that is about to be configured, because fab stamps the
    bootstrap and a rebuild otherwise reuses the copy an earlier build left.

  * conf.d/zz-project-packages replaces the assertion on a literal version,
    which passed on a stale index and let a rebuild ship the previous
    morning's inithooks and confconsole. For each of inithooks, confconsole
    and keel it checks that the archive offers exactly one version, that
    apt's candidate is that version, that the version is served by the
    project archive and not by an upstream source, and that the installed
    package is that candidate and configured. It then removes the build time
    package source, which conf.d/main used to do. A rebuild made after a
    publication now either carries the newly published versions or fails.

 -- Keel Linux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:45:00 +0000

turnkey-nodebb-19.0 (1) turnkey; urgency=low

  * Initial release of the NodeBB appliance for Keel, compatible with
    TurnKey Linux appliances.

  * NodeBB 4.10.3 installed under /var/www/nodebb from the release tarball,
    pinned by version and sha256 in conf.d/main; the last release whose
    dependencies run on Debian's Node.js 20.

  * Node.js 20, npm, Redis 8 and nginx from Debian 13 (Trixie).

  * nginx in front on [::]:443 and [::]:80, proxying to NodeBB on [::1]:4567;
    Redis bound to ::1 and 127.0.0.1.

  * First boot from the instance spec: firstboot.d/40nodebb runs the
    non-interactive NodeBB setup and creates the admin user from
    APP_DOMAIN, APP_EMAIL and APP_PASS.

 -- Keel Linux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
